## 4. ARCHITECTURE

```
[Phone PWA (single index.html, vanilla JS, no build step)]
   │  same-origin
   ├── /api/feeds ........ Vercel serverless fn: fetches 10 RSS feeds server-side (no CORS), returns JSON
   ├── /blog/*.html ...... static published posts (created at runtime via GitHub API)
   ├── /blog/index.json .. posts index (created/updated at runtime via GitHub API)
   ├── /blog/ ............ public blog homepage (static blog/index.html)
   │
   ├── AI providers ...... xAI Grok OR Groq (auto-detected by key prefix), called client-side
   ├── Article scrape .... https://r.jina.ai/{article-url} (CORS-friendly full-text)
   ├── Fallback news ..... 5 public CORS proxies (only if relay missing)
   └── GitHub REST API ... publishes/edits blog files & installs the relay (token stored on device)
```

**Why single-file vanilla frontend:** the owner edits code from a phone via GitHub's mobile editor; no framework, no build, zero-config Vercel.
**No database:** per-device state in `localStorage`; shared content (blog) lives as files in the GitHub repo, served statically by Vercel.

