## 8. NEWS INGESTION PIPELINE

### 8a. Monitored channels (display list, 26)
World(10): Reuters, AP, BBC Breaking, CNN, Al Jazeera, Sky News, Bloomberg, AFP, The Guardian, NBC News.
Africa(10): Africanews, News24 (SA), SABC News, Daily Nation (KE), Citizen Digital (KE), KTN News (KE), Daily Graphic (GH), TimesLIVE (SA), The Africa Report, Jeune Afrique.
Nigeria(6): Channels Television, Arise News, TVC News, Punch, Premium Times, The Cable.

### 8b. Actual feeds pulled (10)
3 Google-News RSS aggregators (`https://news.google.com/rss/search?q=breaking+news[+africa|+nigeria]…`, cap 12 each; source name parsed from `"Title - Source"` suffix) + 7 direct feeds: BBC World (`feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/world/rss.xml`), Al Jazeera (`aljazeera.com/xml/rss/all.xml`), Channels TV (`channelstv.com/feed/`), Punch (`punchng.com/feed/`), Premium Times (`premiumtimesng.com/feed`), SABC (`sabcnews.com/sabcnews/feed/`), Daily Nation (`nation.africa/kenya/rss`), cap 8 each.

### 8c. Relay (`api/feeds.js`, Vercel serverless, CommonJS `module.exports`)
Fetch all 10 feeds **server-side in parallel** (8 s timeout each, custom User-Agent); parse RSS `<item>` (and Atom `<entry>` fallback) with regex; CDATA + entity decode; return `{ok:true, items:[{title,link,pub,region,flag,country,src,goog}]}`; header `Cache-Control: s-maxage=60, stale-while-revalidate=120`.

### 8d. Client gather order
1. `GET /api/feeds` (15 s timeout) → use if items.
2. Else race 5 proxy routes **in parallel per feed** (9 s each): `api.allorigins.win/raw?url=`, `api.allorigins.win/get?url=` (parse `.contents`), `api.rss2json.com/v1/api.json?rss_url=`, `corsproxy.io/?url=`, `r.jina.ai/{feed}`.

### 8e. Rules
- Window: **last 24 h** (fallback: latest few).
- Dedup by hash of link (`seen` list, cap 500, persisted).
- Sort newest-first, cap 60 cards.
- Interval 180 s; manual 🔄 anytime.
- If relay returns 404 → toast hint to install relay; if everything fails → 3 sample cards (`🧪 SAMPLE`).

