## 9. AI GENERATION ENGINE

### 9a. Provider auto-detect & fallback
- Key starts `gsk_` → **Groq** `https://api.groq.com/openai/v1/chat/completions`, models `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` → `llama-3.1-8b-instant`.
- Else **xAI Grok** `https://api.x.ai/v1/chat/completions`, models `grok-3-mini` → `grok-3` → `grok-4` → `grok-2-latest`.
- Try models in order until HTTP 200; 401/403 = hard stop "Key rejected"; `temperature 0.5`.
- `🩺 TEST KEY` pings each model with `max_tokens:5` and prints exact server responses.

### 9b. Input assembly
`GENERATE`: user message = `SOURCE: {source}\nHEADLINE: {title}\nFULL TEXT:\n` + full article scraped via `https://r.jina.ai/{link}` (first 9,000 chars; fallback = headline).
`REGENERATE`: prepends "take a clearly different angle (human vs institutional), never synonym swap" + previous FB text.

### 9c. SYSTEM PROMPT (embed verbatim)
> You are the Senior Breaking News Editor for D-RAY SHOW ("Your Daily Global Update")…
> CORE RULES: treat source as facts only; rebuild from WHO/WHAT/WHERE/WHEN/WHY/HOW; never copy source sentences/structure; never invent facts/quotes/stats; label unverified; lead with the key confirmed development; short punchy sentences; human newsroom tone; banned phrases: "Furthermore, Moreover, In addition, It is worth noting, Interestingly, In today's rapidly changing world, This underscores"; no clickbait; facts→clarity→engagement; sensitive-events language ("police allege", "the suspect").
> CREDIT RULE: `📰 Credit: {Source}`. SIGN-OFF: `📺 D-Ray Show — Your Daily Global Update.` HANDLES appended to social formats.
> OUTPUT: ONLY a JSON object `{`…`}` with exactly 7 plain-text keys:
> - `title`: crafted headline, ≤12 words, no emoji/clickbait.
> - `fb`: line1 title; blank; 🚨 lead; "WHAT WE KNOW SO FAR:" •-bullets; "WHAT HAPPENS NEXT:"; credit; sign-off; follow CTA; 3–5 hashtags incl `#DRayShow`; Meta-policy safe.
> - `tw`: ≤280 chars; fact + status + `📰 via {Source}` + ≤2 hashtags.
> - `vo`: 30 s VO script; timecodes 0:00/0:08/0:16/0:22/0:27; [ON SCREEN] cues (red BREAKING strap + country + logo bug); fixed outro; [END CARD].
> - `cm`: title line; WHY IT MATTERS; THE KEY QUESTION; OUR LINE AS A SHOW.
> - `full`: professional medium blog article, 4–6 flowing paragraphs (~350–500 words); NO labels/headings inside; NO SEO/META/KEYWORDS lines; every fact intact.
> - `ip`: 4:5 image prompt from facts only; brand hexes; logo top-left; BREAKING chip top-right; blue lower-third + red stripe + ≤6-word headline + tagline; `--ar 4:5`.

### 9d. Output parsing (bulletproof)
1. Strip code fences; try `JSON.parse` between first `{` and last `}`.
2. Fallback: locate markers for keys `[title,fb,tw,vo,cm,full,ip]` via regex `["'\*\s\n{,]*KEY["'\*]*\s*:` (case-insensitive), sort by position, slice segments between markers.
3. `cleanVal`: trim; strip surrounding quotes/backticks/asterisks; `\n` literals → newlines; collapse 3+ newlines.
4. `stripBlog`: delete lines starting `SEO TITLE:/META DESCRIPTION:/KEYWORDS:`; strip prefixes like `THE NEWS:` etc. if ever printed.
5. Enforce tweet ≤280 (word-boundary cut + …). Missing `title`/`fb` backfilled.

